<main class="write-main auth-settings"><header class="writer-head"><div><span class="writer-kicker">Account security</span><h1>Sign-in & verification</h1><p>Choose how you verify access to your private workspace.</p></div><a class="wbtn" href="<?=url('/write/security')?>">Devices & passkeys</a></header>
<?php foreach(flashes()as$f):?><p class="notice" role="status"><?=e($f['message'])?></p><?php endforeach;?><?php if($error!==''):?><p class="notice error" role="alert"><?=e($error)?></p><?php endif;?>
<section class="settings-card"><div class="auth-section-heading"><div><span class="writer-kicker">Your access</span><h2><?=$uid===wa_owner_id()?'Super administrator':'Writer account'?></h2></div><span class="auth-badge">Private workspace</span></div><p>These sign-in addresses open the same account and records. New Google or Microsoft identities require a code sent to the approved email before they are linked.</p><ul class="auth-identity-list"><?php foreach(wa_addresses($user)as$email):?><li><strong><?=e($email)?></strong><span><?=$uid===wa_owner_id()?'Super administrator':'Writer'?></span></li><?php endforeach;?></ul></section>
<?php if(!wa_stepup($uid)):?><section class="settings-card auth-stepup"><h2>Verify before making changes</h2><p>Enter your Writer password, then verify with an email code or an enrolled method. This protects changes to your security settings.</p><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="stepup"><label>Current Writer password<input type="password" name="password" autocomplete="current-password" required></label><button class="wbtn primary">Verify my identity</button></form></section><?php else:?><p class="notice" role="status">Identity recently verified. You can manage sign-in methods for 10 minutes.</p><?php endif;?>
<?php if($codes):?><section class="settings-card auth-recovery"><h2>Save your recovery codes</h2><p>These codes are shown once. Store them privately in your password manager. Each code works once after your password or linked provider sign-in.</p><ul><?php foreach($codes as$code):?><li><code><?=e($code)?></code></li><?php endforeach;?></ul></section><?php endif;?>
<div class="auth-settings-grid"><section class="settings-card"><div class="auth-section-heading"><h2>Authenticator app</h2><span class="auth-badge"><?=!empty($factors['totp'])?'Enabled':'Not enrolled'?></span></div><p>Use Microsoft Authenticator, Google Authenticator or another compatible app. Codes work without a mobile signal.</p>
<?php if($setup):$uri='otpauth://totp/'.rawurlencode('Waithaka Ndegwa:'.$user['email']).'?secret='.$setup['secret'].'&issuer='.rawurlencode('Waithaka Ndegwa').'&algorithm=SHA1&digits=6&period=30';?><div class="auth-qr" data-auth-qr="<?=e($uri)?>" aria-label="Authenticator setup QR code"></div><p>Or enter this setup key manually:</p><code class="auth-secret"><?=e($setup['secret'])?></code><p class="login-hint">Time based · 6 digits · 30-second interval. Keep this setup key private.</p><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="totp_finish"><label>Code from your authenticator<input name="code" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]{6}" maxlength="6" autocomplete="one-time-code" required></label><button class="wbtn primary">Confirm authenticator</button></form>
<?php else:?><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><button class="wbtn primary" name="action" value="totp_start" <?=wa_stepup($uid)?'':'disabled'?>><?=!empty($factors['totp'])?'Replace authenticator':'Set up authenticator'?></button></form><?php endif;?>
<?php if(!empty($factors['totp'])):?><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><button class="wbtn" name="action" value="totp_remove" <?=wa_stepup($uid)?'':'disabled'?>>Remove authenticator</button></form><?php endif;?></section>
<section class="settings-card"><div class="auth-section-heading"><h2>Text message</h2><span class="auth-badge"><?=!empty($factors['phone'])?'Number verified':'Not enrolled'?></span></div><p>Verify your own phone before using it for sign-in. An authenticator is the preferred option when mobile delivery is unreliable.</p>
<?php if(!empty($factors['phone'])):?><p>Verified number: <strong>•••• <?=e(substr($factors['phone'],-4))?></strong></p><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><button class="wbtn" name="action" value="phone_remove" <?=wa_stepup($uid)?'':'disabled'?>>Remove verified phone</button></form><?php endif;?>
<?php if(wa_sms_ready()):?><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="phone_start"><label>Mobile number<input type="tel" name="phone" autocomplete="tel" placeholder="+254…" maxlength="16" required></label><button class="wbtn primary" <?=wa_stepup($uid)?'':'disabled'?>>Send setup text</button></form><?php if($phoneSetup):?><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="phone_finish"><label>Text verification code<input name="code" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="one-time-code" maxlength="10" required></label><button class="wbtn primary">Verify phone</button></form><?php endif;?><?php else:?><p class="auth-status-note">Text delivery needs a configured SMS verification service. Email and enrolled authenticators remain available.</p><?php endif;?></section>
<section class="settings-card"><h2>Recovery codes</h2><p><?=count($factors['recovery']??[])?> unused recovery codes. Generating a new set replaces all older codes.</p><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><button class="wbtn" name="action" value="recovery_new" <?=wa_stepup($uid)?'':'disabled'?>>Generate new recovery codes</button></form></section>
<section class="settings-card"><h2>Google & Microsoft</h2><p>Sign in with either provider from the login page. Only basic identity is requested. Calendar, mail and publishing permissions stay in Integrations.</p><?php if(!$identities):?><p>No provider sign-in identity has been linked yet.</p><?php endif;?><?php foreach($identities as$identity):?><article class="auth-identity"><h3><?=e(wa_providers()[$identity['provider']]['name'])?></h3><p><?=e($identity['email'])?></p><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="identity" value="<?=e($identity['key'])?>"><button class="wbtn" name="action" value="unlink" <?=wa_stepup($uid)?'':'disabled'?>>Unlink sign-in identity</button></form></article><?php endforeach;?></section></div>
<?php if($uid===wa_owner_id()):$sms=wa_sms_config();?><details class="settings-card"><summary>Administrator · sign-in service setup</summary><h2>Provider application callbacks</h2><p>Sign-in reuses the existing Google Calendar and Microsoft meeting application callbacks with a separate sign-in state. Keep these exact addresses registered with the corresponding application.</p><?php foreach(wa_providers()as$key=>$provider):?><p><strong><?=e($provider['name'])?></strong> · <?=wa_provider_ready($key)?'Application credentials saved':'Application credentials required'?></p><code class="auth-secret"><?=e(wa_callback($key))?></code><?php endforeach;?><p><a href="<?=url('/write/connections')?>">Manage Google & Microsoft application setup</a></p><h2>SMS verification service</h2><p>Use an existing Twilio Verify service. Saving credentials makes no purchase and sends no message. A text is requested only when a person explicitly verifies their number or chooses text verification.</p><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="sms_settings"><label>Twilio account SID<input name="account" maxlength="34" value="<?=e($sms['account']??'')?>" required></label><label>Verify service SID<input name="service" maxlength="34" value="<?=e($sms['service']??'')?>" required></label><label>Authentication token<input type="password" name="token" autocomplete="new-password" maxlength="200" placeholder="Leave blank to keep the saved token"></label><label class="auth-check"><input type="checkbox" name="enabled" value="1" <?=!empty($sms['enabled'])?'checked':''?>>Enable this service for requested verification texts</label><button class="wbtn primary" <?=wa_stepup($uid)?'':'disabled'?>>Save SMS setup</button></form></details><?php endif;?>
</main><script src="<?=asset('js/vendor/qrcode.js')?>" defer></script><script src="<?=asset('js/writer-auth.js')?>" defer></script>
